+ opts:[
+  {t:'Probes assert current documented behaviour: before, they demonstrated the defect (write ignored, reads COMPARE); after, they verify compliance (CAP bit persists, reads CAPTURE)',c:true, w:'Correct. An audit probe is executable documentation of what the model DOES, wired to the findings table. When the finding moved NON_COMPLIANT → PARTIAL, the probe\'s expected value and docstring flipped with it — same command sequence, opposite assertion.'},
+  {t:'The probe was inverted by mistake and now hides the bug',c:false,w:'There is no bug left to hide: cc_mode genuinely stores CAPTURE. The probe now guards the fix, and the findings entry documents what still isn\'t simulated (event latching).'},
