+ m:`It is created whenever an API exposes two names for one hardware register and the implementer backs each name with its own variable — here, ts.period and ts.capture_compare[0] for the single TAxCCR0. The model can then hold two different "period" values simultaneously, a configuration that has no counterpart in silicon (one set of flip-flops cannot store 1000 and 0 at once).
+It is worse than a missing feature because both paths WORK in isolation: every write round-trips, every read returns something plausible, no error is ever queued. The contradiction only bites when a test or firmware mixes the names — e.g. PWM: duty = CCR1/CCR0. Configure the period via TIMERA0:PERIOD 1000 and duty via CC1:VALUE 250, then compute duty from CC0:VALUE? — you divide 250 by 0. Or worse, each half of the system reads its own store and both look self-consistent.
