+<section>
+<h2>3. The Fix — What Commit a20fbb1 Actually Changed</h2>
+
+<p>Issue #19 covered four findings from the MSP430 compliance audit, all in the Timer_A/Timer_B model, all instances of "the model accepts states silicon can't hold". The commit touched one dataclass and four handlers in <code>silmulator/devices/msp430.py</code>.</p>
+
+<h3>Width enforcement on the counter (TAxR)</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_timer_count</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>, ts: <span class="cls">TimerState</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="add">"""TAxR/TBxR count register (SLAU367P §25.2.1/§26.2.1): 16-bit counter."""</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.is_query:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> str(ts.count)
+    <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.params:
+        <span class="del">ts.count = int(cmd.params[0], 0)</span>              <span class="cm"># BEFORE — any int stored</span>
+        <span class="add">v = int(cmd.params[0], 0)</span>
+        <span class="add"><span class="kw">if not</span> 0 &lt;= v &lt;= 0xFFFF:</span>
+        <span class="add">    <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">222</span>, <span class="str">"Timer count out of range (0-0xFFFF)"</span>)</span>
+        <span class="add">ts.count = v</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">""</span></code></pre>
+
+<p>The identical guard went into <code>_timer_cc_val</code> for the TAxCCRn compare registers (<code>"CCR value out of range (0-0xFFFF)"</code>). Note the check is two-sided: <code>-1</code> is just as unrepresentable in an unsigned 16-bit register as <code>0x10000</code>.</p>
+
+<h3>The CAP bit becomes real stored state</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_timer_cc_mode</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>, ts: <span class="cls">TimerState</span>, cc: int) -> str:
+    <span class="add">"""CAP bit (SLAU367P §25.2.4/§26.2.4): COMPARE or CAPTURE mode.</span>
+
+    <span class="add">Stored state only — no waveform capture is simulated (no edge inputs</span>
+    <span class="add">latch TAxCCRn) since time does not pass in this simulation.</span>
+    <span class="add">"""</span>
+    <span class="add">VALID = {"COMPARE", "CAPTURE"}</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.is_query:
+        <span class="del">return "COMPARE"</span>                       <span class="cm"># BEFORE — writes ignored, constant read</span>
+        <span class="add">return ts.cc_mode.get(cc, "COMPARE")</span>
+    <span class="add"><span class="kw">if</span> cmd.params:</span>
+    <span class="add">    v = cmd.params[0].upper()</span>
+    <span class="add">    <span class="kw">if</span> v <span class="kw">not in</span> VALID:</span>
+    <span class="add">        <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">224</span>, f<span class="str">"Illegal CC mode: {v}"</span>)</span>
+    <span class="add">    ts.cc_mode[cc] = v</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">""</span></code></pre>
+
+<p>Backing it, <code>TimerState</code> gained a per-CC-unit dict — and lost a field (next section):</p>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># TimerState dataclass</span>
+<span class="del">period: int = 0xFFFF</span>                                    <span class="cm"># BEFORE — an independent store</span>
+capture_compare: <span class="cls">Dict</span>[int, int] = field(default_factory=<span class="kw">lambda</span>: {<span class="num">0</span>: <span class="num">0</span>, <span class="num">1</span>: <span class="num">0</span>, <span class="num">2</span>: <span class="num">0</span>, <span class="num">3</span>: <span class="num">0</span>})
+<span class="add">cc_mode: <span class="cls">Dict</span>[int, str] = field(default_factory=<span class="kw">lambda</span>: {<span class="num">0</span>: <span class="str">"COMPARE"</span>, <span class="num">1</span>: <span class="str">"COMPARE"</span>, <span class="num">2</span>: <span class="str">"COMPARE"</span>, <span class="num">3</span>: <span class="str">"COMPARE"</span>})</span></code></pre>
+
+<h3>Four strict xfails flipped to regression guards</h3>
+<p>Exactly as in issue #18, the tests documenting these defects carried <code>@pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True)</code>. The commit deleted four decorators, promoting the tests:</p>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># tests/test_msp430_edge_cases.py — now plain passing tests</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_divider_128_rejected</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §25.2.1.1: no ID x TAIDEX combination produces /128.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"TIMERA0:CLOCK:DIVIDER 128"</span>)
+    <span class="kw">assert</span> <span class="fn">errors</span>(mcu) == <span class="num">1</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_count_over_16bit_rejected_or_masked</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §25.2.1: a 16-bit counter cannot hold 0x10000.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"TIMERA0:COUNT 0x10000"</span>)
+    <span class="kw">assert</span> <span class="fn">errors</span>(mcu) == <span class="num">1</span> <span class="kw">or</span> mcu.timer_a[<span class="num">0</span>].count &lt;= <span class="num">0xFFFF</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_capture_mode_settable</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §25.2.4 (CAP bit): each CC unit supports capture mode.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"TIMERA0:CC1:MODE CAPTURE"</span>)
+    <span class="kw">assert</span> mcu.process(<span class="str">"TIMERA0:CC1:MODE?"</span>) == <span class="str">"CAPTURE"</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_period_is_ccr0_in_up_mode</span>(self, mcu):
